CloudBurrow patch 27 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1340). Applies after patch 0026.

The bug: a column's DEFAULT (CREATE TABLE ... s STRING DEFAULT 'x') was
applied only to an INSERT ... VALUES that left the column out. INSERT ...
SELECT left it NULL, the DEFAULT keyword in VALUES failed "no formatter
registered for ResolvedNodeKind ResolvedNodeKindResolvedDmldefault", and
the catalog kept only the formatted SQLite expression, not the text the
statement wrote, so the emulator could not give the column a
defaultValueExpression. BigQuery uses the default "when the value for a
column is not specified" and "when the keyword DEFAULT is used in place of
the value expression" (https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/default-values).

The patch projects the defaults of the columns an INSERT ... SELECT leaves
out after the query's columns, formats DEFAULT in an INSERT's VALUES as
the column's default (NULL for a column without one; elsewhere, as in
UPDATE ... SET c = DEFAULT, it still fails), and keeps the DEFAULT
clause's text (ResolvedColumnDefaultValue.sql) in ColumnSpec.DefaultSQL.
column_defaults_test.go fails without the patch and passes with it.

